    supervising each binary's WATCH agent — RunAtLoad + WatchPaths, no KeepAlive
    
      reference: yes,yes,yes,--
      swift:     yes,yes,yes,--
      (ran-at-load, re-ran-on-file-change, one-shot-not-resident, log-streams-written)
      launchd's own accounting: ts:runs=1->2:stages=1 swift:runs=1->2:stages=1 
      `stages` is how many times the watched file had to be changed before launchd delivered an
      event. More than 1 is launchd coalescing or dropping a delivery, not a router misbehaving.
    
      note both binaries answered the watch agent's supervision identically this run
           (yes,yes,yes,--), and launchd's own counter is the witness for the one-shot term.
